  "cues": [
    {
      "s": 0.12,
      "e": 4.005,
      "text": "ACR tracks compute prices and helps businesses review"
    },
    {
      "s": 3.9050000000000002,
      "e": 6.117999999999999,
      "text": "their bills. Let\u2019s check one."
    },
    {
      "s": 6.5200000000000005,
      "e": 10.614,
      "text": "The agent calls ACR\u2019s bill checker and rate tool. You"
    },
    {
      "s": 10.514,
      "e": 13.899000000000001,
      "text": "can watch the calls and inspect their results. This example"
    },
    {
      "s": 13.799,
      "e": 17.29,
      "text": "bill is flagged for review, with the recommendation grounded"
    },
    {
      "s": 17.189999999999998,
      "e": 19.019,
      "text": "in the returned evidence."
    },
    {
      "s": 26.52,
      "e": 29.858999999999998,
      "text": "The trace shows the exact amount, quantity, and public"
    },
    {
      "s": 29.759,
      "e": 33.18,
      "text": "price references. Aomi explains that the pricing data"
    },
    {
      "s": 33.08,
      "e": 37.114999999999995,
      "text": "is nearly thirteen days old. It also separates ACR\u2019s"
    },
    {
      "s": 37.015,
      "e": 40.308,
      "text": "index from market prices. A cheaper reference does not"
    },
    {
      "s": 40.208,
      "e": 42.224,
      "text": "automatically authorize payment."
    },
    {
      "s": 47.519999999999996,
      "e": 50.894,
      "text": "The treasury implementation connects that review to on-chain"
    },
    {
      "s": 50.794,
      "e": 54.492999999999995,
      "text": "payments. Aomi provides cloud-hosted contract access"
    },
    {
      "s": 54.393,
      "e": 58.114999999999995,
      "text": "alongside the app\u2019s API tools. A configured deployment"
    },
    {
      "s": 58.015,
      "e": 61.262,
      "text": "checks ownership, funds, budget, and replay protection"
    },
    {
      "s": 61.162,
      "e": 63.131,
      "text": "before preparing a payment."
    },
    {
      "s": 63.586666666666666,
      "e": 67.54166666666667,
      "text": "Here is the actual workflow on GitHub: stage the transaction,"
    },
    {
      "s": 67.44166666666666,
      "e": 71.19866666666667,
      "text": "simulate it, and ask the owner to authorize it. After"
    },
    {
      "s": 71.09866666666667,
      "e": 74.32166666666667,
      "text": "confirmation, verify the receipt and payment event before"
    },
    {
      "s": 74.22166666666666,
      "e": 77.66466666666668,
      "text": "updating the bill. This is implemented code; deployed"
    },
    {
      "s": 77.56466666666667,
      "e": 79.94066666666667,
      "text": "payment acceptance is still pending."
    },
    {
      "s": 80.38666666666667,
      "e": 84.45766666666667,
      "text": "A general-purpose agent framework can call tools. Aomi"
    },
    {
      "s": 84.35766666666666,
      "e": 88.13766666666666,
      "text": "also supplies contract access and the transaction pipeline,"
    },
    {
      "s": 88.03766666666667,
      "e": 91.13266666666667,
      "text": "so the protocol team can focus on its business rules"
    },
    {
      "s": 91.03266666666667,
      "e": 95.39366666666666,
      "text": "instead of assembling the blockchain execution infrastructure."
    },
    {
      "s": 95.85333333333334,
      "e": 99.56433333333334,
      "text": "ACR registers its tools and treasury skill here. The"
    },
    {
      "s": 99.46433333333333,
      "e": 103.16333333333333,
      "text": "frontend imports Aomi\u2019s widget and points it at the app."
    },
    {
      "s": 103.06333333333333,
      "e": 106.47233333333334,
      "text": "That connects the protocol\u2019s workflow to the conversation"
    },
    {
      "s": 106.37233333333333,
      "e": 108.53833333333334,
      "text": "inside its existing interface."
    },
    {
      "s": 108.98666666666668,
      "e": 113.05766666666668,
      "text": "ACR brings the protocol. Aomi connects its APIs and"
    },
    {
      "s": 112.95766666666667,
      "e": 114.51966666666668,
      "text": "contracts for the user."
    }
  ],
